        {
          "title": "Indices and Logarithms",
          "body": "Laws of indices include aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ, aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ, (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ and a⁰ = 1 for non-zero a. A\nlogarithm asks what power a base must be raised to. For example, log₁₀ 1000 = 3."
        }
